(vector (map (:db/id -1)
 (:adr/id "adr-2609078000-kir-is-renamed-osaho")
 (:adr/doc_type "adr")
 (:adr/topic "kir-is-renamed-osaho")
 (:adr/title "kotoba-kir is renamed osaho (筬) — the reed, and nothing else moves")
 (:adr/status "accepted")
 (:adr/date "2026-09-07")
 (:adr/deciders (vector "Jun Kawasaki" "Claude Opus 5"))
 (:adr/repos (vector "com-junkawasaki/root" "kotoba-lang/osaho"))
 (:adr/related (vector "adr-2609076000-kir-is-an-ipld-codec-schema-and-adl" "adr-2609077000-amus-definition-cids-are-unison-shaped-measured" "2608040100" "2608139980"))
 (:adr/body "## Context\n\nThe owner asked for a name in the family's register — beside `kotoba`, `kototama`, `ayatori`, `itonami` — rather than the initialism `kir`, and chose **`osaho`**.\n\nThe family is already named from a loom, so the register was not invented for this: `kotoba` 言葉 (the language), `amu` 編む (the compiler — weaves one closed cloth), `abi` 経 (the warp: WIT / admission contract), 綾 aya (the backends, ADR-2608139980), `kototama` 言霊 (the VM contract).\n\n## Decision\n\n**`kotoba-lang/kotoba-kir` is `kotoba-lang/osaho`.**\n\n筬 (osa) is the reed of a loom. Every warp thread passes through one dent of it, it holds them all in position, and the weft is beaten home against it. It makes nothing and decides nothing; it is what everything passing through must fit. That is the repository: the checked IR every backend shares, and the DefCID they are all keyed on — and its README already states what it does NOT own (parse source, emit code, decide policy).\n\n**The name is coined.** `osaba` 筬羽, `osauchi` 筬打ち and `osatōshi` 筬通し are traditional weaving terms; `osaho` is not. It is recorded as coined rather than presented as traditional, in the README and in the vocabulary entry, because a false etymology in the one place a reader checks is worse than an invented word.\n\n## What moved, and what deliberately did not\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| GitHub repository | renamed. The old name redirects — verified on both the API and the git URL |\n| `manifest/west.yml` | entry `name` and `path`, **two lines**, via the single-entry API commit that is the only correct path for a generated file. The `revision` line was asserted unchanged before and after |\n| `manifest/repos.edn` | the one `:extra-projects` path, rewritten through the EDN reader/writer rather than `sed` — it is a 490 KB one-liner and byte-round-trips |\n| `manifest/concept-vocabulary.edn` | registered, because a name that does not announce its function needs a second entrance (ADR-2608040100) |\n| README | names itself at the top, same rule |\n| **`kotoba.kir.*` namespaces** | **unchanged**, and they remain the API |\n| **every DefCID** | **unmoved** |\n| ~70 consumers' `deps.edn` | **untouched.** `io.github.kotoba-lang/kotoba-kir` git coordinates keep resolving through the redirect |\n\n**No definition identity moved, and the reason is this repository's own guarantee**: names are not in the hash on either side of a call — binders are de Bruijn positions and a callee symbol is replaced by its CID. That was measured on 2026-09-07 (adr-2609077000) before the rename, not assumed after it. A rename that moved DefCIDs would have moved every module lock and compile cache key in the workspace.\n\nThe namespaces stay for the same reason `amu` kept `kotoba.compiler.*`, its `kotoba-compiler/1` wire marker and its `bin/kotoba-compiler` shim after renaming from `compiler`: the repository name is a discovery alias, and the namespace is an API. Moving the API is a separate decision with its own consumers, and this ADR does not make it.\n\n## Naming-rule notes\n\n- **Plane.** `osaho` is a bare **subject**-plane name, where `kotoba-kir` was a `kotoba-` family name. The workspace rule says an existing family's shape takes precedence over elision, and `kotoba-hir`, `kotoba-sema`, `kotoba-wasm`, `kotoba-native`, `kotoba-script`, `kotoba-component` and others keep that shape. **This is a deliberate exception on owner instruction**, with clear precedent in the same area — `amu` (was `compiler`), `kagami` (was `kotoba-fleet-vcs`), `kototama`, `soko`, `ayatori` are all bare metaphor names in `kotoba-lang`. It is not a licence to debadge the rest of the family; that would need its own instruction and its own table.\n- **Names that were already taken** and therefore not available: `ayatori` (kotoba-lang), `tsumugu`, `akashi`, `shirabe` (cloud-itonami), `soko` (kotoba-lang), `tate`. `aze` 綾 was free as a string but rejected because 綾 is the backends' name.\n\n## Follow-up, named rather than done\n\nMigrating the ~70 `deps.edn` coordinates from `io.github.kotoba-lang/kotoba-kir` to `io.github.kotoba-lang/osaho` is a separate wave. It is **not a precondition** — the redirect makes every one of them resolve today — and doing it in the same change would have put a 70-repo edit behind a naming decision. Until it runs, both coordinate names are correct, and a reader who finds `kotoba-kir` in a `deps.edn` is looking at a live dependency, not a broken one.")))
